<div style="width: 100%; background-color: #1a5276; padding: 15px 0; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="color: #ffffff; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Learning to Relax – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="color: #ffffff; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Learning to Balance</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Learning to Relax</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Interactive: Describe the storyline of an audio or visual narrative. Receptive: Demonstrate comprehension of extended discussions on abstract topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can describe the storyline of an audio or visual narrative about balancing school and personal life (e.g., "The speaker shared how they've been balancing their schoolwork with their passion for volunteering.") Can comprehend extended discussions on strategies for learning to relax and maintaining well-being (e.g., "The speaker explained that practicing relaxation techniques like deep breathing and time management is essential for mental health.") Can ask questions about methods for balancing relaxation with daily responsibilities (e.g., "How does the speaker suggest incorporating relaxation into a busy schedule?" "The speaker says that regular relaxation practices help reduce stress and improve overall well-being.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images showing various activities: a student studying intensely, someone doing yoga, friends laughing, a person looking stressed, a person journaling. Students are asked to briefly share which images resonate with their daily lives. The teacher asks: "What do you think 'balance' means in the context of these images?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces key vocabulary words from the audio text: <i>balance, stress, relaxation, mindfulness, wellbeing, schedule, prioritize, unwind, activities, relieve</i>. The teacher models the pronunciation of these words, explicitly focusing on distinguishing the short vowel sound /ɪ/ in "activities" (/ækˈtɪvɪtɪz/) and the long vowel sound /iː/ in "relieve" (/rɪˈliːv/). For example, "Engaging in diverse <b>activities</b> can help <b>relieve</b> daily <b>stress</b>."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If you have a 'balanced schedule,' does that mean you only do one type of activity, or many different ones?" (Expected answer: many different ones, equally distributed).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'mindfulness' about worrying about the future, or paying attention to the present moment?" (Expected answer: paying attention to the present moment).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ / ___ (5-7 min)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students listen to an audio segment (approx. 2-3 minutes) from a podcast titled "Finding Your Calm: A Teen's Guide to Well-being." In the audio, a 17-year-old high school student discusses how she <i>has been juggling</i> her academic workload with her passion for photography and how she incorporates <i>relaxation</i> techniques like <i>mindfulness</i> into her busy <i>schedule</i> to manage <i>stress</i> and maintain her <i>wellbeing</i>. The register is informal but informative, typical of a peer interview or testimonial.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Receptive: Demonstrate comprehension of extended discussions on abstract topics (e.g., mental well-being, stress management strategies). Listening: Interactive: Describe the storyline of an audio narrative (e.g., a student's journey to balance school and relaxation).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (First Listen - Gist):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students listen to the audio once and answer the following gist questions orally: "What is the main topic of the podcast episode?" and "Who is the speaker, and what is her biggest challenge?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Second Listen - True/False): Students listen again to identify whether the following statements are True or False: "The speaker rarely feels stressed about school." "She uses photography as a way to unwind." "She believes practicing mindfulness is not effective for busy students."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ / ___ (10-12 min)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening and Vocabulary)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Identifying key vocabulary related to "Learning to Relax" and "Learning to Balance." Practicing listening for specific details. Applying grammatical structures: Present perfect continuous (ongoing efforts) and Modals for possibility (suggestions).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Listening for Specifics & Gap-fill):</b> The teacher provides a transcript excerpt from the audio with blanks for 5-6 target vocabulary words (e.g., <i>balance, stress, wellbeing, schedule, mindfulness, unwind</i>). Students listen to the audio a third time, filling in the blanks. They then check their answers in pairs. (Example sentence: "I <b>have been</b> trying to find a better __________ between my studies and my hobbies to reduce __________.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Completion with Modals):</b> Teacher writes incomplete sentences on the board incorporating modals for possibility and suggestions, and the present perfect continuous. Students complete them orally, using newly learned vocabulary and ideas from the audio. E.g., "If I had more free time after school, I <b>would</b> __________ to relax." or "To avoid school-related stress, you <b>might</b> need to __________." The teacher guides students to express suggestions and opinions: "You <b>should</b> plan your day better." "I think taking breaks helps me focus."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction (Vocabulary Check & Pronunciation):</b> In pairs, students take turns defining 3-4 of the new vocabulary words to each other in their own words, explicitly ensuring correct pronunciation of 'activities' (/ækˈtɪvɪtɪz/) and 'relieve' (/rɪˈliːv/). They then share one strategy from the audio they found most interesting, explaining why.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ / ___ (15-18 min)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task in a realistic scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Group Discussion and Mini-Presentation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students work in groups of 3-4. Their task is to discuss the audio segment they listened to and identify 2-3 key strategies the speaker uses for balancing her social life, schoolwork, and relaxation. They also need to collectively brainstorm and propose one additional strategy, considering their own cultural perspectives on managing stress and achieving wellbeing. Each group will then prepare a brief (1-2 minute) presentation to another group (or the class) where they will:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Briefly describe the storyline or main points of the audio narrative (e.g., "The speaker shared how she has been balancing...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Present the strategies they identified from the audio, using target vocabulary (e.g., "She suggests practicing <i>mindfulness</i> to <i>unwind</i>, and effectively managing her <i>schedule</i> to maintain <i>balance</i>.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggest their own additional strategy, using modals for possibility (e.g., "We think you <b>might</b> try allocating specific <i>downtime</i> each day to <i>relieve</i> pressure."). They should also express their opinions on the effectiveness of these strategies.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency, collaborative interaction, using target vocabulary and grammar structures in context, describing the audio's narrative, and giving suggestions effectively.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ / ___ (10 min)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment and self-reflection)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on active listening during the podcast, participation in group discussions, use of target vocabulary (<i>balance, stress, relaxation, mindfulness, wellbeing, schedule, prioritize, unwind, activities, relieve</i>), and application of present perfect continuous and modals for suggestions. The teacher notes groups that effectively describe the audio narrative.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The group presentations from Stage 4 serve as the assessment task. The teacher evaluates how well students described the audio's storyline, incorporated specific vocabulary, and used appropriate grammar (e.g., "The speaker explained that practicing relaxation techniques like deep breathing and time management is essential for mental health.") while making suggestions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation, especially of /ɪ/ in "activities" and /iː/ in "relieve."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of at least 5-6 target vocabulary words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence in describing the audio's storyline.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of present perfect continuous and modals for giving suggestions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative interaction within the group.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new strategy for relaxation or balance I learned today from the audio or my classmates is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I feel I can now describe someone's efforts to balance their life (Circle one): Very Well / Moderately Well / A Little."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ / ___ (5-7 min)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompts:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of understanding the audio today, and what helped you overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which new vocabulary word (e.g., mindfulness, wellbeing, procrastinate) will you try to use in your daily conversations about school/life balance this week?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The students successfully identified the main ideas and some specific details from the audio. The pronunciation practice for /ɪ/ and /iː/ was helpful, though some students still need more focused drilling. The group discussion allowed for good interaction, but some groups struggled to integrate the present perfect continuous naturally. I need to provide more explicit sentence starters for complex grammatical structures next time. The introduction of vocabulary for 'downtime' and 'procrastination' was effective for stimulating discussions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> For Lesson 2, students will read a text that expands on the themes and vocabulary introduced today. They will use their listening comprehension skills to build a foundation for understanding the context of the reading material, focusing on how different individuals manage their 'schedule' and avoid 'procrastination' to achieve 'wellbeing'.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ / ___ (3-5 min)</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>